triage: revise_rules: The game behaves as specified, but the scoring makes never guessing dominant. A wrong guess is a 2-point swing (-1 to the guesser, +1 to the code's owner), there are 120 possible codes, four card answers rarely pin one down, and an unguessed code earns its owner +1 each leg. A fixed policy that effectively passes therefore beats random play every time, so the flaw is in the rules, not the file.
